#: ../../source/05-api.rst:40 53e089302ecb4ad59377402e21451ec4
msgid "slimv.analyze"
msgstr ""

#: ce27d6e3bcba46e290be6ac37963de75 of slimv.analyze:1
msgid ""
"`slimv analyze <path>` — inspect a video or a whole library and recommend"
" how to shrink it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/05-api.rst:47 2dbaaf86850d47ef94274b2bf0d002dc
msgid "slimv.check"
msgstr ""

#: 04ffe2a92b174e0193a23da76d1b9a4e of slimv.check:1
msgid ""
"`slimv check <path>` — health scan of a file or folder: report each "
"file's codec, find corrupted/unreadable files, and print summary stats."
msgstr ""

#: 60733540ffee4dcf88cfad98c33386d6 of slimv.check:4
msgid ""
"Unlike :mod:`slimv.verify` (which compares a source tree against a "
"converted tree), ``check`` inspects a single location on its own. Unlike "
":mod:`slimv.analyze` (stats + a re-encode recommendation), ``check`` adds"
" a full-decode integrity pass so it can flag broken files."
msgstr ""

#: 5c5458bac91640858c3293e524fc542c of slimv.check.run:1
msgid "Scan ``path`` (a file or folder) and report codecs, corruption, and stats."
msgstr ""

#: 62630b67f887415d812b233498903713 of slimv.check.run:3
msgid "A video file, or a folder searched recursively."
msgstr ""

#: fc5eca1375c54e9d9a6abad773593443 of slimv.check.run:4
msgid ""
"If True, skip the full-decode integrity pass (ffprobe only — fast, but "
"only catches files that are unreadable at the header)."
msgstr ""

#: 515699a24f8c485988f889d8537cf6ec of slimv.check.run:6
msgid "If True, print a row for every file, not just problems."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/05-api.rst 9c6b0b30f7b94d51be066e37d2ff81e5
msgid "Returns"
msgstr ""

#: 354dc3223fd841cba06833117f1d86fc of slimv.check.run:8
msgid "0 if every file is healthy, 2 if any file is corrupt/unreadable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/05-api.rst:54 796ba4d884174258be4c8dc801844cc4
msgid "slimv.sanity"
msgstr ""

#: d0d2c18834ab44739052b2027784d9bc of slimv.sanity:1
msgid ""
"`slimv test <encoder>` — quick encode+decode sanity check for one "
"encoder, and report whether it ran on hardware or fell back to software."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/05-api.rst:61 a6e9b2a486944c02ae7ef77ee8a965ea
msgid "slimv.benchmark"
msgstr ""

#: 7b394014f92e4ad9918c4cbbb7f2d4b0 of slimv.benchmark:1
msgid ""
"`slimv benchmark <file>` — encode a short sample with several profiles "
"and score each with VMAF, so you can pick quality-vs-size on your own "
"content."
msgstr ""

#: 01b4df0ba4d444f5b52eed1c034810c6 of slimv.benchmark:4
msgid ""
"Method: extract a LOSSLESS reference segment (ffv1), encode that with "
"each profile, then VMAF each output against the lossless reference. "
"Encoding from the same reference guarantees frame-perfect alignment, so "
"the VMAF numbers are trustworthy (no spurious low scores from drift)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/05-api.rst:68 0f86d74a275249028927ec9ae14fba81
msgid "slimv.encode"
msgstr ""

#: be26ad56c5cf4598a833f2fd85735326 of slimv.encode:1
msgid ""
"`slimv encode <src> <dst> --profile <name>` — batch re-encode a tree into"
" a mirrored output tree, verifying and logging every file. Resumable: "
"files whose output already exists are skipped."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/05-api.rst:75 bda3b69b888344e9a582fe2e8691608a
msgid "slimv.verify"
msgstr ""

#: 421d78ea9b0b4d3f92897aa0d3d18e07 of slimv.verify:1
msgid ""
"`slimv verify <src> <dst>` — the deletion safety gate. For every source "
"it confirms the converted file exists, matches the original length, and "
"decodes cleanly. Only files that pass all three are marked SAFE-TO-"
"DELETE. Read-only: it never deletes anything."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/05-api.rst:82 7e8e15f6d7fc41c497ef315f11e3c783
msgid "Support modules"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/05-api.rst:85 0010f04a95c74d8eb092b9a7a45ca5a1
msgid "slimv.profiles"
msgstr ""

#: e16a9ca2080344b7b74c5849983e31d1 of slimv.profiles:1
msgid "Encoding profile catalog."
msgstr ""

#: a00368d034334d05afc69cfde709949f of slimv.profiles:3
msgid ""
"Every profile is a *quality-preserving* recipe: resolution, frame rate "
"and pixel format are left untouched; only the codec/efficiency change. "
"Audio is always re-encoded to AAC 128k (transparent for speech; raise for"
" music)."
msgstr ""

#: c948e05dab89422bb839f54c8cb08073 of slimv.profiles:7
msgid ""
"Rate-control note: for CRF (x265/AV1) and global_quality (QSV) / cq "
"(NVENC), LOWER number = higher quality = bigger file. The numbers are NOT"
" comparable across codecs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/05-api.rst:92 86695fc7964a4709aa6e18b02937289e
msgid "slimv.ffmpeg"
msgstr ""

#: dd6254910ad041138082029007a73596 of slimv.ffmpeg:1
msgid ""
"Thin wrapper around ffmpeg/ffprobe. slimv never encodes itself — it "
"builds command lines and lets ffmpeg do the work, then parses the "
"results."
msgstr ""

#: ceda7a3c874e44f7b237d8bf6d883dc5 of slimv.ffmpeg.run:1
msgid "Run a command. With capture=True, stdout/stderr are returned as text."
msgstr ""

#: c609ae7091be45e4bf01916f4b527283 of slimv.ffmpeg.probe:1
msgid "Full ffprobe JSON (format + streams) or None on failure."
msgstr ""

#: 732b3e562e464b44b5d036e3e30484f3 of slimv.ffmpeg.video_stream:1
msgid "First video stream from a probe() result."
msgstr ""

#: 07b072f319874402b308998b04d28830 of slimv.ffmpeg.vmaf:1
msgid ""
"VMAF mean of `distorted` vs `reference`. Reads the score from ffmpeg's "
"stderr (no log file) to dodge Windows path-escaping issues in the "
"filtergraph. For a trustworthy number the two inputs must be frame-"
"aligned (see benchmark, which encodes from a lossless reference)."
msgstr ""

#: 296028900813413bac13c8c67847135d of slimv.ffmpeg.decode_errors:1
msgid ""
"Full-decode integrity check. Returns the number of error lines ffmpeg "
"emits while reading every frame; 0 == clean."
msgstr ""

#: 6675808e848b4f08a0c299a8604464b6 of slimv.ffmpeg.hardware_impl:1
msgid "Classify a -v verbose encode log as hardware/software/unknown."
msgstr ""

